# Database Standards

## Schema Reference

Before writing any database code, reference:
- `docs/lld/02-database-erd.md` for schema definitions
- `docs/adr/ADR-003-postgresql-database-per-service.md` for database-per-service pattern
- `docs/adr/ADR-006-pool-multi-tenancy-model.md` for multi-tenancy

## Flyway Migrations

```sql
-- V001__create_pipelines_table.sql
-- Every migration MUST be idempotent and reversible where possible

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS pipelines (
    id              UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    tenant_id       UUID NOT NULL,
    name            VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    status          VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'DRAFT',
    created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    updated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    version         INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    
    CONSTRAINT fk_tenant FOREIGN KEY (tenant_id) REFERENCES tenants(id)
);

-- Always create indexes for foreign keys and common queries
CREATE INDEX idx_pipelines_tenant_id ON pipelines(tenant_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_pipelines_status ON pipelines(status) WHERE status = 'ACTIVE';

-- RLS Policy - MANDATORY for all tenant-scoped tables
ALTER TABLE pipelines ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY tenant_isolation ON pipelines
    USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant_id')::uuid);
```

## Row-Level Security (RLS)

```java
// ✅ Always set tenant context before queries
@Component
public class TenantContextSetter {
    private final JdbcTemplate jdbc;
    
    @Transactional
    public void setTenantContext(UUID tenantId) {
        jdbc.execute("SET LOCAL app.current_tenant_id = '" + tenantId + "'");
    }
}

// In service layer
@Transactional
public List<Pipeline> getPipelines(TenantId tenantId) {
    tenantContextSetter.setTenantContext(tenantId.value());
    return repository.findAll();  // RLS automatically filters
}
```

## JPA Entity Pattern

```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "pipelines")
public class PipelineEntity {
    @Id
    private UUID id;
    
    @Column(name = "tenant_id", nullable = false, updatable = false)
    private UUID tenantId;
    
    @Column(nullable = false)
    private String name;
    
    @Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)
    @Column(nullable = false)
    private PipelineStatus status;
    
    @Version  // Optimistic locking - MANDATORY
    private Integer version;
    
    @CreationTimestamp
    @Column(name = "created_at", nullable = false, updatable = false)
    private Instant createdAt;
    
    @UpdateTimestamp
    @Column(name = "updated_at", nullable = false)
    private Instant updatedAt;
}
```

## Query Guidelines

```java
// ✅ Use named parameters
@Query("SELECT p FROM Pipeline p WHERE p.tenantId = :tenantId AND p.status = :status")
List<Pipeline> findByTenantAndStatus(@Param("tenantId") UUID tenantId, @Param("status") String status);

// ✅ Pagination for list queries
Page<Pipeline> findByTenantId(UUID tenantId, Pageable pageable);

// ❌ Never use string concatenation for queries
"SELECT * FROM pipelines WHERE name = '" + name + "'"  // SQL INJECTION RISK
```

## Performance Rules

- Always use `@Version` for optimistic locking
- Create indexes for all foreign keys
- Use partial indexes for status columns
- Paginate all list queries
- Use `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` for complex queries
